  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — the probability of loss — is clearly present in the verbal report: the individual explicitly refers to the 20% chance of receiving nothing in Lottery B. The individual evaluates whether the 1000 Euro gain is sufficient to justify that risk, indicating that they are considering the probability of loss (20%) as a key factor. The decision reason states that the lottery with the lower probability of loss is preferred. Since Lottery A has 0% loss probability and Lottery B has 20%, the reason would prefer A. The individual’s justification — that the gain is not large enough to justify the 20% risk of loss — aligns with the decision reason’s logic of preferring lower probability of loss. Thus, the individual is using the decision reason to justify their choice by comparing the probability of loss between the lotteries. The reasoning is consistent with the rule of the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
